        "original_id": "fa3b7cde-6f09-5b6e-88b1-7247d9781e54",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Thomas Bangalter, Guy-Manuel de Homem-Christo, Gaspar Noé, Monica Bellucci, Vincent Cassel, Albert Dupontel\n- Organizations: Daft Punk, Roulé\n- Projects: Stardust, Together, Irréversible\n- Topics: French house music, film music, non-linear narrative\n\nFacts:\n- Thomas Bangalter founded the French record label Roulé in 1995.\n- Irréversible is a 2002 French art psychological horror drama film written and directed by Gaspar Noé.\n- Irréversible stars Monica Bellucci, Vincent Cassel, and Albert Dupontel.\n- Irréversible uses a non-linear narrative and follows two men through the streets of Paris seeking revenge for a girlfriend who was brutally raped.\n- Thomas Bangalter, born on 3 January 1975, is a French musician, record producer, singer, songwriter, DJ, composer, and film director.\n- Thomas Bangalter is best known as one half of the French house music duo Daft Punk alongside Guy-Manuel de Homem-Christo.\n- Thomas Bangalter also released music as a member of the trio Stardust, the duo Together, and as a solo artist.\n- Thomas Bangalter composed music for the film Irréversible.",
